hello everyone i'm alana and welcome to  my channel where today i am filming from  my iphone  because this is a setup video and i can  really only show you the setup  if i'm not using the setup for context  i'm currently in australia visiting  family because my sister just had a baby  i'm an aunt for the first time  but before i left la where i live i was  like okay  e3 is coming up that's a whole bunch of  streams that i'm going to want to do  i want to make sure that i can still  make youtube content i want to make sure  that i can still  video edit and i definitely have this  conundrum in front of me of like okay  i'm going home for longer than i would  usually go home for because there's also  a two-week quarantine period in a hotel  for you to be able to come to australia  right now so there was this big wall of  obstacles that i wasn't sure how to  approach  as someone who generally just does all  of that  from a beefy pc so i had to do some  brainstorming to make sure that i could  travel  and still play games still stream  still video edit video editing probably  being one of the hardest hurdles there  from anywhere i'm also jumping between  three houses i go from my mom's house to  my dad's house sometimes to my sister's  place  but obviously also the hotel room so  this needed a lot of mobility  and initially i just really wasn't sure  how i was going to manage  but this is what it looks like right now  i am at my mom's place this is my mom's  office with this  giant calculator she has up there  but this right here is  my remote streaming setup this  is it i'm currently uploading a video it  does take a little bit longer in  australia than it would  otherwise but first things first very  easy microphone solution that i find  very easy to move  is the elgato wave 3. the reason that i  like this microphone so much especially  for traveling is because it's really  modular  meaning that it's very easy for me to  take this whole thing apart to remove  the base to remove the stand and to  remove the top  uh to make it very easy to put into a  backpack it's also great sound quality  and also  acts as a sound mixer the elgato wave 3  comes with a software called  the wavelink that allows you to if  you're streaming streamers will know  what i'm talking about when i talk about  this  it allows you to have different channels  for different things so i can have  discord and one channel  my game audio and another channel which  is generally just desktop sounds  and then my microphone in a third  channel so if i want to edit any streams  down  they're not all on the same track now go  to away 3 has been awesome  this is a little bit more of a refined  version than what i have at home i  usually have a mic  arm i also have a filter on it but  for on the go this is great so easy to  be with so easy to pack down it fits  into a really small pocket in my bag  it's wonderful  next up here i have already made a video  about this but this is the razer  keo pro now the reason that this webcam  i think is so helpful for me um  obviously if you want to have something  that's even more stripped back you could  use the built-in  webcam on a laptop but the reason that i  really like the keo pro  is because it's a really good camera for  low light um dramatically  uh improved compared to the previous  webcam that i was using  um and i don't have a lighting setup  that was a choice that i made  was i wasn't gonna bring a light with me  you could bring a portable light you  could  um get you know a small ring light that  you would attach on a tripod if you're  traveling that's not that hard to do  but i made the decision that i wasn't  going to do that and was instead just  going to use  the razer keyo pro generally i'm using  natural lighting so things work out okay  but a lot of my e3 streams  were at like 3 am because  on australian time that's just the way  watching e3 press conferences really  goes  okay so that's the webcam next up is my  portable  monitor setup this beautiful thing right  here  is actually very interesting let me show  you guys  how this thing works okay so this  is the mobile pixel us um  and it is a screen that attaches to the  back of my razor it connects through  usb-c it's in the side of the screen and  then connects  at the back of the laptop and can be  used in a bunch of  like if i want to show you guys what i'm  looking at like a presentation style  it pivots backwards so i could do that i  could flip it directly to the back i  could pop it out to the side  pretty much tons of options with this  thing so  it is actually um a screen that that  slides back into this case  and magnetizes to the back of your  laptop  there are four magnets that i have that  are stuck to the back of the laptop  the screen you stick on here  and then you slide this out now the  reason that this has been particularly  um  important for me is not only does it  make video editing very easy because i  have my premiere pro on this main screen  and all my files  on this side screen it's also really the  only reason that i can  successfully twitch stream without  needing another backup monitor  i have my game running on here  obs running on here in a smaller screen  and then the chat  running on here as well so my main  screen is how i play the video  game the side screen is how i see my  recordings  and the chat and all my stream setup  it's awesome for that these two together  are just um  perfect so of course last but not least  is my razer blade 15.  this thing can run cyberpunk uh disco  elysium  cell attack conspiracy um i've also  played a bunch of gmod i played dungeons  and dragons on it  and for the most part capable of running  those games at the same time  as running obs i am running a six core  intel core i7  nvidia geforce rtx 3070 laptop  gpu fhd 144hp hertz  512 gigs of storage 16 gigabytes of ram  an advanced heat pipe razer chroma  gigabit internet  and it's only 19.9 millimeters  it definitely gets weightier when you  have the the mobile pixel screen on the  back of it  but for the most part is a very  lightweight  easy to carry tidy laptop portability  um compared to the functionality is  incredible premiere pro  on my pc at home just keeps on crashing  on me  or it'll freeze for a while i have not  had any of those problems  on the razor blade whatsoever i am very  happy with it and for how simple this  whole setup is  i fitted the whole thing into a backpack  i break down the microphone  i fold up the laptop and it all fits in  one backpack that's carry-on on a plate  everything has worked so smoothly and i  guess there's also  kind of an extra upside to this whole  setup  is that you can really do it  anywhere and i mean anywhere  it's lovely  and that is it for me today everyone it  feels very weird to have shot a video  mostly on my phone for the first time in  ages  with the intention of showing you guys  this wonderful setup that i have here  but that really is everything if anyone  has any more questions please do let me  know  because i am so so so glad to have found  this setup  and have not had any problems in the  last two months  really at all thank you all for watching  i will see you guys next time
 

